## $\chi^2$ Test of Goodness of Fit Example

$$ \chi^2 = \sum_{j=0}^{J} \frac{(O_j – N\pi_j)^2}{N\pi_j} = \sum_{j=0}^{J} \frac{(O_j – E_j)^2}{E_j} $$

::: fragment

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
obs_chisq <- (65 - 20)^2 / 20 +
  (10 - 20)^2 / 20 +
  (5 - 20)^2 / 20 +
  (5 - 20)^2 / 20 +
  (15 - 20)^2 / 20
obs_chisq
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 130
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code}
obs_chisq > chisq_crit
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] TRUE
```


:::
:::

:::

[We can reject the null in favor of the alternative that the number of students is not the same across majors.]{.fragment}

## R Function

::: fragment

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
admissions_data <- read.csv(here::here("lab", "data", "gatech_admissions.csv"))

admissions_data_2025 <- admissions_data |>
  filter(year == 2025)

chisq <- admissions_data_2025 |>
  select(applied) |>
  chisq.test()
