## $\chi^2$ Test of Independence Example

$$ \chi^2 = \sum_{j=0}^{J} \frac{(O_j – N\pi_j)^2}{N\pi_j} = \sum_{j=0}^{J} \frac{(O_j – E_j)^2}{E_j} $$

::: fragment
:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="66%"}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="false"}
data.frame(type = c("Undergrad", "Graduate", "Total"),
           `In-State` = c(25, 5, 30),
           `Out-of-State` = c(10, 10, 20),
           Total = c(35, 15, 50)) 
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
       type In.State Out.of.State Total
1 Undergrad       25           10    35
2  Graduate        5           10    15
3     Total       30           20    50
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="false"}
chisq_crit <- qchisq(.95, df = (2 - 1) * (2 - 1))
chisq_crit
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 3.841459
```


:::
:::

:::

::: {.column width="33%"}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="false"}
obs_chisq <- (25 - 21)^2 / 21 +
  (10 - 14)^2 / 14 +
  (5 - 9)^2 / 9 +
  (10 - 6)^2 / 6
obs_chisq
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
[1] 6.349206
```


:::

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="false"}
obs_chisq > chisq_crit
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
